## Draft Results paragraph

Across the 1,157 clubs in the eligible transfer network, the median club had two distinct sending partners, two distinct receiving partners and one partner with transfers in both directions (Figure 1a). Mean in-degree and out-degree were both 9.52, reflecting the presence of clubs with many more partners than the median. This variation describes the transfer routes observed across both age groups and all recorded seasons. It gives context for the next comparison, which tests whether transfers involving players aged 30 or older entered the Premier League less often than expected when age labels are shuffled within the same origin club and season.
